    "timingType": "Simplex timing chain. The OM642 utilizes a single-row timing chain. While generally robust, it is known to stretch at higher mileages (250,000+ km), especially if oil change intervals are stretched. Listen carefully for cold-start rattle. The timing chain tensioner should be considered a wear item.",
    "injectionType": "Common-Rail Direct Injection (CDI) with highly advanced Piezo injectors operating at up to 1600 bar. This late-facelift iteration represents the final and most refined version of the OM642 in the W212, perfectly matching its torque delivery to the new 9-speed transmission.",
    "engineLifespan": "300 000 - 500 000+ km. The core mechanical block of the OM642 V6 is phenomenally strong. The true lifespan of the engine is entirely dictated by the maintenance of its complex peripherals: the infamous oil cooler seals, the BlueTEC AdBlue system, and the DPF/EGR components.",
    "turboType": "Single Variable Nozzle Turbine (VNT). The Garrett variable geometry turbocharger provides massive low-end torque with zero lag. The electronic turbo actuator is prone to failure, often caused by heat soak or oil dripping from a failing PCV valve directly above it.",
    "ecuType": "Bosch EDC17. A highly complex ECU managing not only the engine but the entire SCR (Selective Catalytic Reduction) AdBlue system. It responds incredibly well to software tuning.",
    "euroStandard": "Euro 6",
    "maxPowerStockInternals": "350+ hp. The internal forged connecting rods and crankshaft are heavily over-engineered. The limitation is never the block, but rather the thermal limits of the turbocharger and the flow capacity of the DPF.",
