    "timingType": "Simplex timing chain located at the REAR of the engine block. The OM651 timing chain is highly controversial due to its placement. While it can last 200,000+ km with strict oil changes, chain stretch requires dropping the engine or transmission to replace. Listen closely for a metallic rattle on cold starts.",
    "injectionType": "Common-Rail Direct Injection (CDI) up to 2000 bar. Early pre-facelift models were plagued by catastrophic Delphi piezo injector failures. Most were recalled and replaced with solenoid units, but verifying this is absolutely critical before purchase.",
    "engineLifespan": "300 000 - 500 000+ km. The cast iron block is exceptionally durable and capable of immense mileage. The true lifespan is entirely dictated by the maintenance of the rear timing chain and the complex sequential bi-turbo system.",
    "turboType": "Sequential Twin-Turbo (Bi-Turbo). Features a smaller high-pressure turbo for instantaneous response and a larger low-pressure turbo for top-end power. The transition is managed by complex vacuum actuators that frequently degrade and leak.",
    "ecuType": "Bosch EDC17 / Delphi CRD. A highly complex ECU managing the complex twin-turbo transitions and fuel injection. It is incredibly receptive to software tuning, safely unlocking V6-levels of torque.",
    "euroStandard": "Euro 5 / Euro 6",
    "maxPowerStockInternals": "280+ hp. The internal forged connecting rods and crankshaft are heavily over-engineered. The block itself handles increased boost effortlessly, limited only by the thermal capacity of the twin-turbo setup.",
    "fuelConsumption": {
      "city": "6.0 - 7.5 L/100km",
      "highway": "4.5 - 5.5 L/100km",
      "mixed": "5.0 - 6.2 L/100km",
      "sporty": "7.5+ L/100km"
    },
    "oilSpecification": "6.5L 5W-30 Fully Synthetic Low-SAPS (MB 229.51 or 229.52). Using Low-SAPS is strictly mandatory to prevent catastrophic DPF clogging and to protect the delicate rear timing chain.",
    "commonIssues": [
      "Timing Chain Stretch: The OM651 engine famously locates its simplex timing chain at the rear of the block, making access incredibly difficult. Due to its single-row design, it stretches over high mileages, leading to a failing tensioner. You will hear a distinct, sharp metallic rattle on cold starts when this occurs.",
      "Delphi Piezo Injector Failure: Early OM651 250 CDI models were plagued by catastrophic failures of the Delphi piezo injectors. These would fail without warning, completely disabling the engine and leaving drivers stranded. Most were replaced under a massive recall with solenoid units, but verification is absolutely essential.",
      "Bi-Turbo Vacuum System Leaks: The sequential twin-turbocharger system relies on a complex web of vacuum lines and actuators to transition between turbos. These rubber lines degrade and crack from extreme engine heat over time. This leads to severe boost leaks, sluggish acceleration, and Limp Mode engagement.",
      "Water Pump and Coolant Leaks: The engine utilizes a complex array of plastic coolant flanges and a water pump housing that become brittle with heat. These frequently develop hairline cracks, leading to slow but persistent coolant loss. Catching these leaks early is vital to prevent severe engine overheating.",
      "Intake Manifold Swirl Flaps: The plastic swirl flaps inside the intake manifold accumulate heavy soot and oil sludge from the EGR system. Eventually, the actuator linkages break or the flaps seize completely. This drastically reduces performance and throws the car into Limp Mode.",
      "DPF Pressure Sensor: The differential pressure sensor monitoring the Diesel Particulate Filter fails with alarming regularity on this chassis. When this happens, the ECU cannot trigger regenerations, leading to a rapidly clogging filter. It is a relatively cheap part that can cause massive peripheral damage if ignored."
    ],
    "vulnerabilities": [
      "Engine-Out Timing Chain Repair: Because the timing chain is positioned practically against the firewall, what is a standard maintenance task becomes a massive financial burden. Mechanics often must drop the transmission or the entire engine just to replace the chain. Neglecting the chain stretch will result in pistons destroying the valves.",
      "Bi-Turbo Complexity Costs: The sequential turbo system offers incredible performance but doubles the potential points of mechanical failure. Diagnosing a boost leak requires tracing dozens of vacuum lines and testing multiple individual actuators. Replacing the entire turbo assembly itself is vastly more expensive than the single-turbo variants.",
      "Delphi Stranding Risk: If the car is somehow still running original Delphi piezo injectors, it is a ticking time bomb. When an injector shorts out, the ECU completely shuts off the fuel pressure to protect the engine. You will instantly lose all power on the highway and require an emergency tow.",
      "Catastrophic Coolant Loss: The plastic water pump and coolant flanges can fail without much warning, dumping coolant rapidly. If the driver ignores the temperature gauge, the aluminum cylinder head will warp under the intense heat. This necessitates an incredibly expensive top-end engine rebuild.",
      "Intake Manifold Replacement: A simple, cheap plastic swirl flap linkage failure cannot be fixed with an OEM patch kit. Mercedes requires you to purchase an entirely new intake manifold assembly to solve the issue. This cascades a minor wear issue into a significant parts and labor bill.",
      "DPF Blockage from Urban Driving: The OM651 absolutely requires regular highway driving to achieve the high exhaust temperatures needed for DPF regeneration. Strict urban commuting will cause the filter to fatally clog with dense soot. A clogged DPF creates immense backpressure, ultimately destroying the turbocharger assembly."
    ],
