    "compression": "10.7:1",
    "yearRange": "2009-2011",
    "timingType": "Double-roller chain. The M273 engine in the W212 generation was manufactured after the infamous balance shaft/idler gear soft-metal defect was resolved mid-2008. Therefore, it is generally safe from catastrophic timing failures, though the chain tensioner should still be monitored at high mileages.",
    "injectionType": "Multi-Point Sequential Fuel Injection (ME-SFI). Mercedes-Benz retained traditional port injection for this naturally aspirated V8. This is a massive blessing for long-term reliability, as it completely avoids the severe carbon buildup on intake valves that plagues later direct-injected engines.",
    "engineLifespan": "250 000 - 400 000+ km. The core aluminum block with Silitec cylinder linings is incredibly robust. The true lifespan of the vehicle is largely dictated by the longevity of the AirMatic suspension, the intake manifold flaps, and the 7G-Tronic transmission.",
    "turboType": "Naturally Aspirated. The 5.5-liter V8 breathes entirely on its own, utilizing a complex dual-stage variable intake manifold. It provides instant, lag-free throttle response and a remarkably smooth, linear power delivery that perfectly suits an executive cruiser.",
    "ecuType": "Bosch ME 9.7. A highly advanced ECU that controls the continuous variable valve timing on all four camshafts and the variable intake manifold. It provides extensive diagnostic capabilities and is very receptive to mild naturally aspirated tuning.",
    "euroStandard": "Euro 5",
    "maxPowerStockInternals": "500+ hp. The internal rotating assembly is very strong. While it doesn't have the forged pedigree of an AMG engine, it can handle significant naturally aspirated tuning and mild forced induction without opening the block.",
    "fuelConsumption": {
      "city": "16.0 - 18.5 L/100km",
      "highway": "8.5 - 10.5 L/100km",
      "mixed": "11.5 - 13.0 L/100km",
      "sporty": "17.0+ L/100km"
    },
    "oilSpecification": "8.5L 5W-40 or 0W-40 Fully Synthetic (MB 229.5). High-quality synthetic oil is absolutely vital to protect the four camshafts and variable valve timing phasers. Frequent 10,000 km oil changes are highly recommended.",
    "commonIssues": [
      "Intake Manifold Tumble Flap Breakage: The plastic levers that actuate the variable intake runners become brittle from engine heat and snap off completely. This causes a poor, erratic idle, triggers the check engine light, and drastically reduces low-end torque.",
      "Camshaft Adjuster Solenoid Leaks: The seals on the four camshaft magnets at the front of the engine frequently leak oil over time. This oil can wick directly into the engine wiring harness, traveling all the way to the ECU.",
      "AirMatic Suspension Failure: The heavy 5.5L V8 rapidly wears out the front AirMatic air struts and the main suspension compressor. The rubber air bladders develop micro-tears, causing the car to sag when parked overnight.",
      "Engine Mount Collapse: The immense weight and torque of the V8 engine crush the fluid-filled engine mounts surprisingly fast. When they fail, harsh vibrations are transferred directly into the cabin, especially noticeable when idling in gear.",
      "7G-Tronic Conductor Plate Issues: The internal speed sensors on the 722.9 transmission conductor plate are prone to failing, particularly on early W212 models. This forces the transmission into Limp Mode, locking it in second gear until the car is restarted.",
      "Thermostat Failure: The electronically mapped thermostat frequently fails in the open position, preventing the engine from reaching its optimal 100°C operating temperature. This leads to poor fuel economy, increased emissions, and accelerated engine wear over time."
    ],
    "vulnerabilities": [
      "Intake Manifold Replacement Cost: Because Mercedes does not sell the external plastic actuator lever separately, a broken flap linkage usually dictates replacing the entire intake manifold assembly. This turns a cheap plastic failure into a massive parts and labor bill.",
      "ECU Destruction via Oil Wicking: If the leaking camshaft magnets are ignored, capillary action will draw the oil through the wiring harness directly into the main engine control unit. Once the ECU is flooded with oil, it shorts out and requires complete, highly expensive replacement.",
      "AirMatic Stranding: A catastrophic blowout of an AirMatic strut will instantly drop the car's ride height to the bump stops, rendering it completely undrivable. Towing a slammed W212 without causing further undercarriage damage is extremely difficult.",
      "Transmission Shudder: The 722.9 automatic transmission requires absolute religious adherence to 60,000 km fluid change intervals. If neglected, the torque converter clutch will glaze and begin to shudder violently under moderate acceleration.",
      "Secondary Air Injection Pump Burnout: A stuck relay can cause the secondary air injection pump to run continuously until it physically burns out and melts its housing. This triggers a permanent check engine light and causes the car to fail emissions testing.",
      "Rear Subframe Corrosion: Early W212 models suffer from a notorious factory defect where the rear subframe rusts violently from the inside out. In severe cases, the rear suspension control arms can literally tear away from the chassis while driving."
    ],
