    "timingType": "Double-roller chain. By the time the W212 was introduced, Mercedes had completely resolved the disastrous M272 balance shaft soft-metal sprocket issue. The timing chain and balance shaft in this generation are highly robust and generally last the lifetime of the engine.",
    "injectionType": "Stratified Direct Injection (CGI). Utilizes highly advanced Piezo-electric injectors and a mechanical high-pressure fuel pump (HPFP). While this greatly improves fuel economy and power over the port-injected models, it introduces massive risks of intake valve carbon buildup and expensive HPFP failures.",
    "engineLifespan": "200 000 - 350 000+ km. The core aluminum block is virtually indestructible. However, the lifespan and running costs are heavily dictated by the direct injection system. HPFP failures and severe carbon buildup are the primary lifespan limiters of the CGI variant.",
    "turboType": "Naturally Aspirated. The 3.5L V6 provides a very smooth, linear power delivery. Without turbo lag, throttle response is instantaneous, making it an excellent highway cruiser.",
    "ecuType": "Bosch MED17.7.1. A highly complex ECU managing the incredibly fast Piezo injectors and stratified charge modes. Diagnosing CGI faults requires specialized STAR diagnostic equipment.",
    "euroStandard": "Euro 5",
    "maxPowerStockInternals": "350+ hp. The internal rotating assembly is very strong. However, naturally aspirated tuning yields very modest gains, usually capped around 310 hp with software and exhaust modifications.",
    "fuelConsumption": {
      "city": "12.0 - 14.5 L/100km",
      "highway": "7.5 - 9.0 L/100km",
      "mixed": "8.5 - 10.5 L/100km",
      "sporty": "15.0+ L/100km"
    },
    "oilSpecification": "8.0L 5W-40 or 0W-40 Fully Synthetic (MB 229.5). Strict adherence to 10,000 km oil change intervals is mandatory to protect the delicate high-pressure fuel pump lobes and variable valve timing phasers.",
    "commonIssues": [
      "High-Pressure Fuel Pump (HPFP) Failure: The mechanical HPFP driven by the camshaft is the Achilles heel of the CGI engine. It frequently wears out, causing extended cranking times, severe power loss, and Limp Mode. It is an exceptionally expensive part to replace.",
      "Intake Manifold Tumble Flap Breakage: The plastic levers that actuate the variable intake runners become brittle from engine heat and snap off completely. This causes a poor, erratic idle and drastically reduces low-end torque. Mercedes only sells the entire manifold.",
      "Direct Injection Carbon Buildup: Because fuel is injected directly into the cylinders, it never washes over the intake valves. Over time, thick, tar-like carbon sludge builds up on the valves, causing misfires and restricting airflow. Professional walnut blasting is required.",
      "Camshaft Adjuster Solenoid Leaks: The seals on the four camshaft magnets at the front of the engine frequently leak oil over time. This oil can wick directly into the engine wiring harness, traveling all the way to the main ECU.",
      "NOx Sensor Failures: The stratified charge combustion process produces high nitrogen oxides, requiring complex NOx sensors in the exhaust. These sensors degrade rapidly from heat and soot, triggering the check engine light and requiring costly replacements.",
      "Thermostat Failure: The electronically mapped thermostat frequently fails in the open position, preventing the engine from reaching its optimal 90°C operating temperature. This leads to poor fuel economy and accelerated engine wear."
    ],
    "vulnerabilities": [
      "Financial Ruin via HPFP Replacement: The CGI-specific high-pressure fuel pump is notoriously fragile and carries a staggering replacement cost. If it fails internally, it can also leak raw fuel into the engine oil, destroying the engine bearings.",
      "Intake Manifold Replacement Cost: Because Mercedes does not sell the external plastic actuator lever separately, a broken flap linkage usually dictates replacing the entire intake manifold assembly. This turns a cheap plastic failure into a massive parts and labor bill.",
      "ECU Destruction via Oil Wicking: If the leaking camshaft magnets are ignored, capillary action will draw the oil through the wiring harness directly into the main engine control unit. Once the ECU is flooded with oil, it shorts out and requires complete replacement.",
      "Carbon Choking: Neglecting intake valve cleaning will eventually cause the engine to misfire violently and lose significant compression. The carbon chunks can also break off and damage the delicate exhaust valves or catalytic converters.",
      "Transmission Conductor Plate Failure: The internal speed sensors on the 722.9 transmission conductor plate are prone to failing. This forces the transmission into Limp Mode, locking it in second gear until the car is restarted.",
      "Rear Subframe Corrosion: Early W212 models suffer from a notorious factory defect where the rear subframe rusts violently from the inside out. In severe cases, the rear suspension control arms can literally tear away from the chassis while driving."
    ],
