    "oilSpecification": "Approx. 5.5-6.0L 5W-40 or 0W-40 fully synthetic engine oil meeting suitable Mercedes-Benz petrol-engine approvals.",
    "commonIssues": [
      "Thermostat and cooling-system faults are among the most commonly discussed M274 weak points and can cause slow warm-up, unstable temperature control, or reduced refinement.",
      "Carbon buildup on the intake side is a normal direct-injection ageing issue and can gradually worsen cold-start quality, throttle response, and idle smoothness.",
      "PCV / crankcase ventilation faults can lead to rough idle, oil-consumption changes, vacuum-related running issues, and unstable mixture behavior.",
      "Timing-chain wear, tensioner ageing, and timing-related startup noise can appear, especially on poorly serviced or high-mileage examples.",
      "Ignition-coil and spark-plug wear can produce hesitation, misfires, poor cold running, and reduced smoothness under load.",
      "Oil leaks from upper-engine sealing points, breather-related areas, and surrounding components can appear with age and complicate diagnosis if neglected.",
      "Turbocharger and charge-air-system faults can cause lazy boost response, whistle changes, oily pipework, or weak mid-range pull.",
      "Camshaft actuator / solenoid-related issues are also mentioned among known M274 family problem points and can affect timing behavior and drivability.",
      "9G-TRONIC gearbox ageing can add rough shifts, delayed engagement, or calibration-related drivability complaints if servicing has been neglected."
    ],
    "vulnerabilities": [
      "The biggest vulnerability is that the engine has relatively little displacement reserve, so small faults affect drivability more noticeably than on larger engines.",
      "Long oil intervals are especially harmful because they increase risk for timing wear, internal deposits, and general top-end deterioration.",
      "Short-trip use accelerates carbon buildup, incomplete warm-up wear, and gradual loss of smoothness.",
      "Cooling-system neglect is more damaging than many owners expect because the engine depends heavily on stable thermal control to feel refined.",
      "Weak diagnostics are dangerous because ignition, boost, breather, timing, and cooling faults can imitate one another.",
      "Cheap ignition parts, poor-quality sensors, or lazy breather repairs can quickly ruin the polished factory behavior of the drivetrain.",
      "A short test drive can flatter the car, because a slightly tired M274.910 may still feel good enough at light throttle.",
      "Because this is a market-specific tax-optimized version, parts lookup and exact configuration verification by VIN may matter more than on mainstream E-Class variants."
    ],
