    "timingType": "Simplex timing chain. The OM642 utilizes a single-row timing chain. While generally robust, it is known to stretch at higher mileages (250,000+ km), especially if oil change intervals are stretched. Listen carefully for cold-start rattle. The timing chain tensioner should be considered a wear item.",
    "injectionType": "Common-Rail Direct Injection (CDI) with highly advanced Piezo injectors operating at up to 1600 bar. This final iteration of the OM642 V6 features the most refined fueling mapping but is heavily reliant on a strict AdBlue (SCR) system.",
    "engineLifespan": "300 000 - 500 000+ km. The core mechanical block of the OM642 V6 is phenomenally strong and virtually immortal. The true lifespan is entirely dictated by the maintenance of its complex peripherals: the infamous oil cooler seals, the BlueTEC AdBlue system, and the DPF/EGR components.",
    "turboType": "Single Variable Nozzle Turbine (VNT). The Garrett variable geometry turbocharger provides massive low-end torque with zero lag. The electronic turbo actuator is prone to failure, often caused by heat soak or oil dripping from a failing PCV valve directly above it.",
    "ecuType": "Bosch EDC17. A highly complex ECU managing not only the engine but the incredibly strict SCR (Selective Catalytic Reduction) AdBlue system. It responds incredibly well to software tuning, safely unlocking significant power.",
