    "timingType": "Chain. The updated OM654M still utilizes a timing chain located at the REAR of the engine block. While chain durability has been slightly improved, stretching can still occur at high mileages if oil changes are neglected, requiring an expensive engine-out or transmission-out repair.",
    "injectionType": "Common-Rail Direct Injection (CDI) operating at an immense 2700 bar. This heavily updated engine integrates a 48V Integrated Starter Generator (ISG) sandwiched between the engine and transmission, providing EQ Boost mild-hybrid assistance and allowing seamless engine-off coasting.",
    "engineLifespan": "250 000 - 450 000+ km. The all-aluminum block with Nanoslide cylinder coating is exceptionally durable. However, the true lifespan is heavily dictated by the rigorous maintenance of its highly condensed, heat-soaked emissions systems (DPF, dual-EGR, SCR), the rear timing chain, and the new 48V hybrid system.",
    "turboType": "Sequential Twin-Turbo (BiTurbo). Features a smaller high-pressure turbocharger for instant response and a larger low-pressure turbo for top-end power. The 48V ISG completely masks any remaining turbo lag by instantly filling the torque gap.",
    "ecuType": "Bosch MD1. An incredibly advanced engine control unit that manages the 2700 bar fuel injection, twin turbos, ultra-strict emissions monitoring, and the complex 48V EQ Boost ISG system. It is heavily locked down.",
    "euroStandard": "Euro 6d-ISC-FCM",
    "maxPowerStockInternals": "330+ hp. The internal forged rotating assembly is incredibly strong. The block can handle significant boost increases, with the primary limitation being the hypersensitive DPF/SCR monitoring systems and the 48V ISG integration limits.",
    "fuelConsumption": {
      "city": "6.0 - 7.5 L/100km",
      "highway": "4.5 - 5.5 L/100km",
      "mixed": "5.0 - 6.0 L/100km",
      "sporty": "8.0+ L/100km"
    },
    "oilSpecification": "6.5L 5W-30 Fully Synthetic Low-SAPS (MB 229.52). Absolute adherence to strict 10,000 km oil change intervals is mandatory to protect the rear timing chain, the delicate twin-turbos, and prevent DPF clogging.",
    "commonIssues": [
      "48V ISG (EQ Boost) Failure: The Integrated Starter Generator is highly complex. If the 48V system fails, the car loses its starter motor, alternator, and hybrid assist entirely. Replacing the ISG requires removing the transmission and is a terrifyingly expensive dealership repair.",
      "Rear Timing Chain Stretch: The OM654M retains the rear-mounted timing chain. Due to its single-row design, it stretches over high mileages if oil changes are stretched. You will hear a distinct, sharp metallic rattle on cold starts.",
      "Camshaft Rocker Arm Wear: While slightly mitigated in the OM654M, the rapid wear of the camshaft rocker arms (roller cam followers) remains a risk if oil quality degrades, causing severe camshaft damage and a loud ticking noise.",
      "Engine-Mounted DPF/SCR Thermal Stress: To heat up the emissions system quickly, the DPF and SCR catalyst are bolted directly to the engine block. This subjects the surrounding sensors and wiring to extreme, constant heat soak, accelerating their failure.",
      "Complex AdBlue (SCR) System Failures: The dual-dosing AdBlue system is incredibly complex. The NOx sensors frequently degrade from heat and soot, triggering dashboard countdowns that will eventually prevent the car from starting.",
      "Switchable Water Pump Issues: The engine uses a switchable water pump to bring the engine up to temperature rapidly. The internal shroud mechanism can jam over time due to coolant degradation. This leads to localized overheating.",
      "48V Battery Degradation: The compact 48V lithium-ion battery in the trunk degrades over time. When it fails, the entire EQ Boost system shuts down, throwing the car into Limp Mode."
    ],
    "vulnerabilities": [
      "48V System Immobilization: If the 48V battery or ISG fails, the car does not revert to a normal diesel. Because the ISG acts as the starter motor, the vehicle will be completely immobilized and refuse to start, requiring a tow to the dealership.",
      "Engine-Out Timing Chain Repair: Because the timing chain is positioned practically against the firewall, mechanics must drop the transmission or the entire engine just to replace the chain. Neglecting the chain stretch will result in pistons destroying the valves.",
      "Catastrophic Valvetrain Failure: If rocker arm wear occurs and is ignored, the camshaft lobes will literally grind themselves flat against the seized roller followers. A complete camshaft and lifter replacement is a massively expensive, labor-intensive repair.",
      "AdBlue No-Start Countdown: If the ECU detects any fault in the incredibly sensitive SCR system, it initiates a hard countdown. Once the permitted number of miles or starts reaches zero, the ECU completely immobilizes the vehicle.",
      "DPF Blockage from Urban Commuting: The OM654M relies on extreme exhaust temperatures to actively burn off trapped soot in the DPF. If the car is used strictly for short city trips, these regenerations are constantly aborted. The filter will fatally clog.",
      "Transmission Torque Overload: The massive 550 Nm of torque plus the instant electric punch from the ISG places immense strain on the 9G-Tronic transmission. Bypassing the strict 120,000 km fluid service interval guarantees premature clutch pack failure."
    ],
