      "PCV / crankcase ventilation faults can lead to rough idle, oil-consumption changes, vacuum-related running issues, and unstable mixture behavior.",
      "Timing-chain wear, tensioner ageing, and timing-related startup noise can appear, especially on poorly serviced or high-mileage examples.",
      "Camshaft actuator or timing-control-related faults can affect smoothness, fault memory, and general drivability.",
      "Ignition-coil and spark-plug wear can create hesitation, misfires, poor cold running, and reduced smoothness under load.",
      "Oil leaks from upper-engine sealing points, breather-related areas, and surrounding components can appear with age and complicate diagnosis if ignored.",
      "Turbocharger and charge-air-system faults can cause lazy boost response, whistle changes, oily pipework, or weaker-than-expected mid-range pull.",
