    "timingType": "Chain. The M256 utilizes a complex timing chain system located at the REAR of the engine block. While generally highly robust, stretching can occur at very high mileages if oil changes are neglected, requiring a massive engine-out or transmission-out repair. Listen closely for a metallic rattle on cold starts.",
    "injectionType": "Direct Injection with highly precise Piezo injectors. This engine is a technological tour de force, abandoning front accessory belts entirely. The water pump and AC compressor are electrically driven by the 48V system.",
    "engineLifespan": "200 000 - 400 000+ km. The all-aluminum inline-6 block with Nanoslide cylinder coating is mechanically bulletproof. The true lifespan of the vehicle is heavily dictated by the rigorous maintenance of its incredibly complex 48V ISG hybrid system and the rear-mounted timing chain.",
    "turboType": "Single Exhaust Gas Turbocharger + Electric Auxiliary Compressor (eZV). This brilliant setup completely eliminates turbo lag. The electric compressor spins to 70,000 RPM in 300 milliseconds to provide instant boost while the exhaust-driven turbocharger spools up for massive top-end power.",
    "ecuType": "Bosch MG1. An incredibly advanced engine control unit that manages the direct injection, the exhaust turbo, the electric compressor, and the complex 48V EQ Boost ISG system. It is heavily locked down but remains receptive to high-end ECU tuning.",
    "euroStandard": "Euro 6d-ISC-FCM",
    "maxPowerStockInternals": "550+ hp. The internal forged rotating assembly is incredibly strong and perfectly balanced. The block can handle significant boost increases, with the primary limitation being the 48V ISG integration limits and the transmission clutches.",
    "fuelConsumption": {
      "city": "10.0 - 12.0 L/100km",
      "highway": "7.0 - 8.5 L/100km",
      "mixed": "8.0 - 9.5 L/100km",
      "sporty": "14.0+ L/100km"
    },
    "oilSpecification": "8.0L 5W-30 Fully Synthetic Low-SAPS (MB 229.52). Absolute adherence to strict 10,000 km oil change intervals is mandatory to protect the rear timing chain, the exhaust turbocharger, and the Nanoslide cylinder walls.",
    "commonIssues": [
      "48V ISG (EQ Boost) Failure: The 48V Integrated Starter Generator is highly complex and known to fail. Because it acts as both the starter motor and alternator, its failure leaves the car completely immobilized. Diagnosing the issue often requires a dealer, and replacement involves removing the transmission.",
      "Electric Auxiliary Compressor (eZV) Faults: The electric supercharger that eliminates turbo lag operates under immense stress. When the internal electronics or bearings fail, the car experiences severe hesitation off the line and instantly triggers Limp Mode.",
      "Rear Timing Chain Wear: The M256 places the timing chain at the rear of the engine block to save space. While robust, stretching at high mileages requires dropping the engine or transmission to replace it, turning a wear item into a massive labor bill.",
      "Direct Injection Carbon Buildup: As a direct-injected engine, fuel does not wash over the intake valves to keep them clean. Carbon sludge builds up rapidly on the valves, causing rough idling, misfires, and restricted airflow that requires professional walnut blasting.",
      "48V Battery Degradation: The dedicated 48V lithium-ion battery in the trunk is extremely sensitive to deep discharging and heat. When it degrades, it disables the entire EQ Boost hybrid system, throwing terrifying dashboard warnings and refusing to start the car."
    ],
    "vulnerabilities": [
      "48V System Immobilization: Because the car completely lacks a traditional 12V starter motor, any failure in the 48V ISG or the trunk-mounted battery means the engine absolutely cannot be started. The vehicle becomes an instant brick, requiring a flatbed tow and an incredibly expensive dealership visit.",
      "Engine-Out Timing Chain Repair: The rear-mounted timing chain turns standard high-mileage maintenance into a financially devastating repair. Mechanics must completely remove the engine and transmission from the car just to replace the chain and tensioners, generating immense labor hours.",
      "Transmission Torque Overload: The combined torque of the inline-6 and the instant 250 Nm punch from the electric motor places immense strain on the 9G-Tronic transmission. Bypassing the strict 120,000 km fluid service interval guarantees premature torque converter and clutch pack failure.",
      "eZV Supercharger Replacement Cost: The electric auxiliary compressor is a highly proprietary, sealed unit that cannot be rebuilt. If the internal electronics or bearings fail, owners are forced to buy a brand new, highly expensive unit directly from Mercedes-Benz.",
      "Cylinder Wall Scoring (Nanoslide): The M256 uses Nanoslide-coated aluminum cylinder walls that are extremely sensitive to poor lubrication or oil dilution. If oil change intervals are stretched or a fuel injector leaks, the cylinder walls will score deeply, requiring a complete engine rebuild."
    ],
