    "timingType": "Chain. The M274 utilizes a single-row timing chain. It is highly prone to stretching over high mileages, and the hydraulic tensioners frequently lose pressure, causing a distinct metallic rattle on cold starts. Preventative tensioner replacement is strongly recommended.",
    "injectionType": "Direct Injection with advanced Piezo injectors operating at up to 200 bar. This is combined with an 88-horsepower electric motor integrated into the transmission. The direct-injected nature introduces a severe risk of carbon buildup on the intake valves over time.",
    "engineLifespan": "150 000 - 250 000+ km. The M274 block has a controversial reliability record due to infamous wrist pin failures on early models. The true lifespan is heavily dictated by rigorous oil changes to combat hybrid oil dilution and the health of the high-voltage battery.",
    "turboType": "Single Exhaust Gas Turbocharger. It provides excellent low-end torque, which is further supplemented by the instant electric punch of the PHEV motor, effectively eliminating any perceived turbo lag.",
    "ecuType": "Bosch MED17.7.2 combined with a sophisticated Hybrid Control Module. The system seamlessly juggles pure electric gliding, regenerative braking, and gasoline power. It is heavily locked down but receptive to specific hybrid-optimized tuning.",
    "euroStandard": "Euro 6c",
    "maxPowerStockInternals": "350+ hp. The internal rotating assembly is notorious for weak wrist pins on early iterations. Pushing massive boost increases on the stock internals without verifying the wrist pin revision is highly dangerous.",
    "fuelConsumption": {
      "city": "2.5 - 4.5 L/100km (With charged battery)",
      "highway": "6.5 - 8.0 L/100km (Depleted battery)",
      "mixed": "4.5 - 6.5 L/100km",
      "sporty": "10.0+ L/100km"
    },
    "oilSpecification": "6.5L 5W-40 Fully Synthetic MB 229.5. Absolute adherence to strict 8,000 km oil change intervals is mandatory to combat the severe oil dilution caused by frequent engine start-stop cycles in hybrid mode.",
    "commonIssues": [
      "M274 Wrist Pin Wear: The wrist pins connecting the pistons to the rods have improper factory tolerances. They wear prematurely, causing a severe metallic knocking sound on startup. This requires immediate engine teardown to prevent complete destruction.",
      "High-Voltage Battery Degradation: The lithium-ion pack in the trunk loses capacity over thousands of charge cycles. This severely limits the pure electric range and triggers hybrid system faults. Replacing the battery is an incredibly expensive dealership procedure.",
      "Timing Chain Rattle: The M274 utilizes a single-row timing chain that stretches over high mileages. The hydraulic tensioners also lose pressure, causing a distinct rattle on cold starts. Ignoring this leads to timing correlation faults and potential engine damage.",
      "PCV Valve Oil Ingestion: The crankcase ventilation valve is highly prone to failing and passing excessive oil vapor. This coats the entire intake tract in oil, exacerbating direct injection carbon buildup. It must be replaced preventatively to protect the engine.",
      "Water Pump Failure: The engine-driven water pump features a plastic impeller that degrades and cracks from heat cycles. This leads to sudden coolant loss and potential engine overheating. Upgrading to a metal impeller pump is highly recommended.",
      "Electric A/C Compressor Failure: The PHEV uses a high-voltage AC compressor to cool the cabin when the engine is off. This compressor operates under massive electrical load and frequently burns out. Replacing it requires specialized high-voltage training and expensive OEM parts.",
      "Direct Injection Carbon Buildup: Because fuel is injected directly into the cylinders, it never washes over the intake valves. Thick, tar-like carbon sludge builds up on the valves, causing misfires and restricting airflow. Professional walnut blasting is required at higher mileages."
    ],
    "vulnerabilities": [
      "Catastrophic Cylinder Scoring: If the infamous wrist pin issue is ignored, the loose pins will carve deep grooves into the cylinder walls. This destroys the engine block entirely, resulting in massive oil consumption and zero compression. A full engine replacement is the only viable cure.",
      "Hybrid System Immobilization: If the high-voltage battery, inverter, or the hybrid control module fails, the car does not simply revert to a standard gasoline engine. The entire vehicle will refuse to start, leaving you completely stranded. The proprietary nature of these components makes independent repairs impossible.",
      "Severe Oil Dilution: The frequent, short run-times of the gasoline engine during hybrid operation prevent the oil from reaching optimal temperatures to burn off moisture. This severe oil dilution drastically reduces lubrication, accelerating wear on the main bearings and timing chain. Strict 8,000 km oil changes are absolutely critical.",
      "Catastrophic Timing Chain Jump: If the cold-start chain rattle is ignored for too long, the timing chain will physically stretch beyond the tensioner's limits. The chain will eventually jump teeth on the camshaft sprockets, causing the pistons to strike the open valves. This instantly destroys the engine and necessitates a complete replacement.",
      "PTC Heater Burnout: The E 350 e utilizes a high-voltage PTC electric heater to warm the cabin during pure electric driving. This heating element is notoriously fragile and frequently burns out, leaving the car without heating. It is a highly labor-intensive component to access and replace under the dashboard.",
      "AirMatic Suspension Collapse: The heavy gasoline engine paired with the massive high-voltage battery places immense strain on the optional AirMatic suspension. The front struts frequently develop leaks in the airbags, causing the car to sag directly onto the tires overnight. Replacing the struts with aftermarket units is mandatory to avoid burning out the compressor."
    ],
