    "commonIssues": [
      "Elevated oil consumption can still appear on M254-family engines and should be watched carefully between services, especially on higher-output applications.",
      "Timing-chain rattle at cold start or adaptation-related timing concerns should be taken seriously, particularly on cars with stretched oil intervals.",
      "48V mild-hybrid support faults can affect start-stop behavior, restart quality, warning-state frequency, and the smooth low-speed polish expected of a premium drivetrain.",
      "Electric coolant-pump and thermal-management issues can create fault codes, inconsistent warm-up behavior, and expensive secondary heat-related risks.",
      "Carbon buildup on the intake side remains a normal direct-injection ageing issue and can gradually reduce smoothness and response.",
      "Ignition-coil and spark-plug wear can create hesitation, rough cold starts, and reduced refinement under load.",
      "PCV / crankcase ventilation faults can lead to unstable idle, oil-consumption changes, and mixture-control irregularities.",
      "Turbocharger actuator, charge-air leak, or boost-control faults can make the car feel less seamless and less strong than it should, especially during overtaking.",
      "9G-TRONIC shift quality still depends on proper service history and can undermine the luxury character of the whole car if neglected.",
      "Because this version feels strong in stock form, buyers may overlook subtle drivability flaws that they would notice more quickly on a weaker calibration."
    ],
    "vulnerabilities": [
      "The biggest vulnerability is that the stronger calibration can hide moderate deterioration because the car still feels brisk enough to impress on a short drive.",
      "Long oil intervals are especially harmful because the engine still depends heavily on clean oil for timing health, deposit control, and oil-consumption stability.",
      "Short-trip use can accelerate intake deposits, incomplete warm-up wear, and gradual erosion of the polished low-speed behavior that makes the E 300 feel expensive.",
      "Cooling-system neglect is especially dangerous because this drivetrain relies on stable mapped heat management and multiple electrically controlled components.",
      "Weak diagnostics are costly because ignition, thermal, oil-consumption, boost, and 48V support issues can overlap without one dramatic smoking gun.",
      "Poor-quality fuel, deferred maintenance, or careless tuning are more likely to dull this version because it operates with a broader torque and performance envelope.",
      "Because the car feels naturally stronger than the E 200, owners may drive through early warning signs longer before realizing the drivetrain is no longer at its best."
    ],
