      "Short-trip use is not automatically harmless just because the car is a plug-in hybrid; repeated cold petrol-engine cycles can still accelerate contamination and carbon-related ageing.",
      "Battery-cooling and thermal-management neglect is expensive because both halves of the drivetrain depend on stable temperature control and fault-free circulation.",
      "Weak diagnostics are particularly costly because petrol, charging, HV battery, 12V support, electrical, and transmission-side issues can overlap very convincingly.",
      "Cars that were rarely charged can still drive acceptably, but they often lose a big part of what makes the E 300 e worthwhile in the first place.",
