    "timingType": "Chain. The OM654M utilizes a simplex timing chain located at the REAR of the engine block. While chain durability has been slightly improved, stretching can still occur at high mileages if oil changes are neglected, requiring an expensive engine-out or transmission-out repair.",
    "injectionType": "Common-Rail Direct Injection (CDI) operating at an immense 2700 bar. This heavily updated engine (OM654M) features an increased displacement and integrates a 2nd-generation 48V Integrated Starter Generator (ISG) sandwiched between the engine and transmission.",
    "engineLifespan": "250 000 - 450 000+ km. The all-aluminum block with Nanoslide cylinder coating is exceptionally durable. However, the true lifespan is heavily dictated by the rigorous maintenance of its highly condensed emissions systems (DPF, dual-SCR), the rear timing chain, and the new 48V ISG hybrid system.",
    "turboType": "Single Variable Nozzle Turbine (VNT) with Water Cooling. The updated OM654M turbo features a water-cooled bearing housing for longevity. The 48V ISG completely masks any turbo lag by instantly filling the torque gap off the line.",
    "ecuType": "Bosch MD1. An incredibly advanced engine control unit that manages the 2700 bar fuel injection, ultra-strict Euro 6e emissions monitoring, and the complex 48V EQ Boost ISG system. It is heavily locked down with state-of-the-art tuning protection.",
    "euroStandard": "Euro 6e",
    "maxPowerStockInternals": "280+ hp. The internal forged rotating assembly is incredibly strong, featuring a new crankshaft to achieve the 1993 cc displacement. The primary limitation is the hypersensitive DPF/SCR monitoring systems and the 48V ISG integration limits.",
    "fuelConsumption": {
      "city": "5.5 - 6.5 L/100km",
      "highway": "4.2 - 5.0 L/100km",
      "mixed": "4.8 - 5.5 L/100km",
      "sporty": "7.5+ L/100km"
    },
    "oilSpecification": "6.5L 5W-30 Fully Synthetic Low-SAPS (MB 229.52). Absolute adherence to strict 10,000 km oil change intervals is mandatory to protect the rear timing chain, the delicate rocker arms, and prevent DPF clogging.",
    "commonIssues": [
      "48V ISG (EQ Boost) Failure: The 2nd-generation Integrated Starter Generator is highly complex. If the 48V system fails, the car loses its starter motor, alternator, and hybrid assist entirely. Replacing the ISG requires removing the transmission and is a terrifyingly expensive dealership repair.",
      "Rear Timing Chain Stretch: The OM654M retains the rear-mounted timing chain. Due to its single-row design, it stretches over high mileages if oil changes are stretched. You will hear a distinct, sharp metallic rattle on cold starts.",
      "Camshaft Rocker Arm Wear: While slightly mitigated in the OM654M, the rapid wear of the camshaft rocker arms (roller cam followers) remains a risk if oil quality degrades, causing severe camshaft damage and a loud ticking noise.",
      "Engine-Mounted DPF/SCR Thermal Stress: To heat up the emissions system quickly, the DPF and dual SCR catalysts are bolted directly to the engine block. This subjects the surrounding sensors and wiring to extreme, constant heat soak.",
      "Complex AdBlue (SCR) System Failures: The dual-dosing AdBlue system is incredibly complex to meet Euro 6e. The NOx sensors frequently degrade from heat and soot, triggering dashboard countdowns that will eventually prevent the car from starting."
    ],
    "vulnerabilities": [
      "48V System Immobilization: If the 48V battery or ISG fails, the vehicle will be completely immobilized and refuse to start, requiring a tow to the dealership. It cannot be bump-started or bypassed.",
      "Engine-Out Timing Chain Repair: Because the timing chain is positioned practically against the firewall, mechanics must drop the transmission or the entire engine just to replace the chain. Neglecting the chain stretch will result in pistons destroying the valves.",
      "Catastrophic Valvetrain Failure: If rocker arm wear occurs and is ignored, the camshaft lobes will literally grind themselves flat against the seized roller followers. A complete camshaft and lifter replacement is a massively expensive, labor-intensive repair.",
      "AdBlue No-Start Countdown: If the ECU detects any fault in the incredibly sensitive SCR system, it initiates a hard countdown. Once the permitted number of miles or starts reaches zero, the ECU completely immobilizes the vehicle.",
      "Transmission Torque Overload: The torque from the diesel combined with the instant electric punch from the ISG places immense strain on the 9G-Tronic transmission. Bypassing the strict 120,000 km fluid service interval guarantees premature clutch pack failure."
    ],
