    "yearRange": "2023-Present",
    "timingType": "Chain. The OM654M utilizes a simplex timing chain located at the REAR of the engine block. While generally robust, stretching can occur at high mileages if oil changes are neglected, requiring an expensive engine-out or transmission-out repair. Listen closely for a metallic rattle on cold starts.",
    "injectionType": "Common-Rail Direct Injection (CDI) operating at an immense 2700 bar. This model integrates a massive 129 hp electric motor sandwiched between the engine and the 9G-Tronic transmission, supported by a very large ~25.4 kWh high-voltage battery pack allowing up to 100km of pure electric range.",
    "engineLifespan": "250 000 - 450 000+ km. The all-aluminum block with Nanoslide cylinder coating is exceptionally durable. However, the true lifespan is heavily dictated by the rigorous maintenance of its highly condensed emissions systems, the rear timing chain, and the incredibly complex High-Voltage (HV) battery system.",
    "turboType": "Single Variable Nozzle Turbine (VNT). The electric motor provides massive, instant low-end torque, negating the need for complex multi-turbo setups. The transition between pure electric and diesel-electric power is managed seamlessly by the ECU.",
    "ecuType": "Bosch MD1 combined with a highly sophisticated 4th Generation Hybrid Control Module. The system seamlessly juggles pure electric gliding, stop-start events, and full diesel-electric torque delivery. It is heavily locked down due to the hybrid integration and Euro 6e compliance.",
    "euroStandard": "Euro 6e",
    "maxPowerStockInternals": "350+ hp. The internal forged rotating assembly is incredibly strong. The primary limitation is entirely the hybrid inverter system, the high-voltage battery discharge limits, and the transmission wet clutch integration.",
    "fuelConsumption": {
      "city": "0.5 - 2.0 L/100km (With charged battery)",
      "highway": "4.5 - 6.0 L/100km (Depleted battery)",
      "mixed": "1.5 - 3.5 L/100km",
      "sporty": "7.5+ L/100km"
    },
    "oilSpecification": "6.5L 5W-30 Fully Synthetic Low-SAPS (MB 229.52). Absolute adherence to strict 10,000 km oil change intervals is mandatory to protect the rear timing chain, the delicate turbo, and combat the severe oil dilution caused by PHEV operation.",
    "commonIssues": [
      "High-Voltage Battery Degradation: The massive ~25.4 kWh lithium-ion battery pack degrades over time due to constant deep cycling. As capacity drops, pure electric range diminishes. Replacing the HV battery out of warranty is a financially devastating repair.",
      "Extreme DPF Clogging (PHEV Specific Flaw): Because the W214 can drive up to 100km purely on electricity, the diesel engine never gets hot enough to perform a DPF regeneration during typical urban use. This leads to the DPF fatally clogging with soot much faster than standard diesel models.",
      "Electric Heater & AC Compressor Failure: The PHEV utilizes a high-voltage electric heater (PTC) and an electric AC compressor to provide cabin climate control when the diesel engine is off. These high-voltage components frequently fail, disabling climate control entirely and requiring expensive dealership replacements.",
      "Rear Timing Chain Stretch: The OM654M locates its timing chain at the rear of the block, making access incredibly difficult. It stretches over high mileages if oil changes are stretched. You will hear a distinct, sharp metallic rattle on cold starts.",
      "Camshaft Rocker Arm Wear: A critical flaw in the OM654 architecture is the rapid wear of the camshaft rocker arms (roller cam followers). If oil changes are neglected, these rockers wear down, causing severe camshaft damage and a loud ticking noise.",
      "Complex AdBlue (SCR) System Failures: The dual-dosing AdBlue system is incredibly complex to meet Euro 6e. The NOx sensors frequently degrade from heat and soot, triggering dashboard countdowns that will eventually prevent the car from starting."
    ],
    "vulnerabilities": [
      "Hybrid System Immobilization: If the high-voltage battery, inverter, or the hybrid control module fails, the car does not simply revert to a standard diesel. The entire vehicle will refuse to start, leaving you completely stranded. Independent shops often cannot perform these repairs.",
      "Severe Oil Dilution: The frequent, short run-times of the diesel engine during hybrid operation prevent the engine oil from reaching optimal temperatures to burn off moisture and unburnt fuel. This severe oil dilution drastically reduces lubrication, accelerating wear on the main bearings and rear timing chain.",
      "Engine-Out Timing Chain Repair: Because the timing chain is positioned practically against the firewall, what is a standard maintenance task becomes a massive financial burden. Mechanics often must drop the transmission or the entire engine just to replace the chain.",
      "Catastrophic Valvetrain Failure: If the rocker arm wear is ignored, the camshaft lobes will literally grind themselves flat against the seized roller followers. A complete camshaft and lifter replacement is a massively expensive, labor-intensive repair.",
      "AdBlue No-Start Countdown: If the ECU detects any fault in the incredibly sensitive SCR system, it initiates a hard countdown. Once the permitted number of miles or starts reaches zero, the ECU completely immobilizes the vehicle."
    ],
