    "timingType": "Chain. The OM656M features a complex timing chain system located at the REAR of the engine block. While generally highly robust compared to 4-cylinders, stretching can occur at high mileages if oil changes are neglected, requiring a massive engine-out or transmission-out repair.",
    "injectionType": "Common-Rail Direct Injection (CDI) operating at an immense 2700 bar. This heavily updated engine (OM656M) features an increased displacement (2989 cc) and integrates a 2nd-generation 48V Integrated Starter Generator (ISG) sandwiched between the engine and transmission.",
    "engineLifespan": "300 000 - 500 000+ km. The inline-6 aluminum block with steel pistons is exceptionally durable. The true lifespan of the vehicle is largely dictated by the maintenance of the highly complex emissions systems (DPF, dual-SCR), the rear timing chain, and the new 48V ISG hybrid system.",
    "turboType": "Sequential Twin-Turbo (BiTurbo). Features a smaller high-pressure turbocharger for instant response and a larger low-pressure turbo for massive top-end power. The 48V ISG completely masks any turbo lag by instantly filling the torque gap off the line.",
    "ecuType": "Bosch MD1. An incredibly advanced engine control unit that manages the 2700 bar fuel injection, twin turbos, ultra-strict Euro 6e emissions monitoring, and the complex 48V EQ Boost ISG system. It is heavily locked down with state-of-the-art tuning protection.",
    "euroStandard": "Euro 6e",
    "maxPowerStockInternals": "450+ hp. The internal forged rotating assembly is incredibly strong, featuring a new crankshaft to achieve the 2989 cc displacement. The primary limitation is the hypersensitive DPF/SCR monitoring systems and the 48V ISG integration limits.",
    "fuelConsumption": {
      "city": "7.5 - 9.0 L/100km",
      "highway": "5.0 - 6.5 L/100km",
      "mixed": "6.0 - 7.5 L/100km",
      "sporty": "9.5+ L/100km"
    },
    "oilSpecification": "8.5L 5W-30 Fully Synthetic Low-SAPS (MB 229.52). Absolute adherence to strict 10,000 km oil change intervals is mandatory to protect the rear timing chain, the delicate twin-turbos, and prevent DPF clogging.",
    "commonIssues": [
      "48V ISG (EQ Boost) Failure: The 2nd-generation Integrated Starter Generator is highly complex. If the 48V system fails, the car loses its starter motor, alternator, and hybrid assist entirely. Replacing the ISG requires removing the transmission and is a terrifyingly expensive dealership repair.",
      "Rear Timing Chain Stretch: The OM656M retains the rear-mounted timing chain architecture. Prolonged oil change intervals can lead to chain elongation and tensioner wear. A metallic rattle on cold start is a critical warning sign that requires immediate attention.",
      "Camtronic Variable Valve Timing Faults: The advanced Camtronic system allows variable exhaust valve lift to heat up the SCR catalyst faster. The electronic actuators for this system can stick or fail due to intense heat cycles, leading to erratic idling and Limp Mode.",
      "Engine-Mounted DPF/SCR Thermal Stress: To heat up the emissions system quickly, the DPF and dual SCR catalysts are bolted directly to the engine block. This subjects the surrounding sensors and wiring to extreme, constant heat soak.",
      "Tandem Oil/Vacuum Pump Leaks: The engine uses a combined oil and vacuum pump located at the rear of the block. The internal seals can fail, leading to oil leaking down the bellhousing, often misdiagnosed as a rear main seal leak."
    ],
    "vulnerabilities": [
      "48V System Immobilization: If the 48V battery or ISG fails, the vehicle will be completely immobilized and refuse to start, requiring a tow to the dealership. It cannot be bump-started or bypassed.",
      "Engine-Out Timing Chain Repair: Because the timing chain is positioned practically against the firewall, mechanics must drop the transmission or the entire engine just to replace the chain. Neglecting the chain stretch will result in pistons destroying the valves.",
      "AdBlue No-Start Countdown: If the ECU detects any fault in the incredibly sensitive SCR system, it initiates a hard countdown. Once the permitted number of miles or starts reaches zero, the ECU completely immobilizes the vehicle.",
      "DPF Blockage from Urban Commuting: The OM656M relies on extreme exhaust temperatures to actively burn off trapped soot in the DPF. If the car is used strictly for short city trips, these regenerations are constantly aborted. The filter will fatally clog, creating massive backpressure that can destroy the twin turbochargers.",
      "Transmission Torque Overload: The massive 750 Nm of torque from the diesel combined with the instant electric punch from the ISG places immense strain on the 9G-Tronic transmission. Bypassing the strict 120,000 km fluid service interval guarantees premature clutch pack failure."
    ],
