    "timingType": "Simplex chain drive located at the rear of the engine block. The OM654M engine family retained the firewall-side chain layout, making maintenance highly complicated. With proper lubrication and 10,000-kilometer oil changes, the chain is durable, but the risk of stretching has not completely disappeared.",
    "injectionType": "Common-Rail direct diesel injection with an operating pressure of 2700 bar. Features piezo-electric injectors and a 48-volt integrated starter-generator system. Due to the Euro 6e standard, it is characterized by enhanced emission control.",
    "engineLifespan": "250 000 - 450 000+ km. The combination of an aluminum block and steel pistons theoretically results in a highly durable structure. The true lifespan will be limited by the condition of the complex hybrid components and environmental peripherals.",
    "turboType": "Single variable geometry turbocharger with a water-cooled bearing housing. The response time of the charger is excellent, and the presence of turbo lag is completely eliminated in practice by the torque fill of the integrated starter-generator.",
    "ecuType": "Bosch MD1. A highly complex engine control unit that works in close connection with the hybrid powertrain controller and transmission control modules. Its software protection represents one of the most advanced levels in the industry.",
    "euroStandard": "Euro 6e",
    "maxPowerStockInternals": "280+ hp. The mechanical foundations and internal forged components have serious reserves. Software performance increases are first limited by the thermal capacity of the particulate filter and the sensitivity of the AdBlue system.",
