    "commonIssues": [
      "48-volt starter-generator failure. Electrical disturbances of the integrated ISG unit and its associated hybrid control modules can occur unexpectedly. This failure completely prevents the internal combustion engine from starting.",
      "Elongation of the rear simplex chain. Due to improper oil change intervals, the timing chain can stretch prematurely. The looseness of the chain and the pressure loss of the tensioner cartridge cause metallic rattling noises during cold starts.",
      "Premature wear of the roller rocker arms. The rollers located in the cylinder head can seize in the event of inadequate lubrication. This wear becomes continuous and long-term, causing damage to the camshaft lobes.",
      "Dual-dosing SCR AdBlue system faults. Due to Euro 6e regulations, AdBlue injection has become incredibly complex. NOx sensors and dosing units are prone to failure due to high temperatures.",
      "Seizing of the vacuum-controlled switchable water pump. The internal blocking element regulating the coolant circulation can get stuck. This mechanical fault results in localized overheating or excessively slow engine warm-up.",
      "Intake side soot buildup. Due to direct injection and EGR recirculation, the intake tracts become dirty. The thick layer of soot reduces engine performance and causes an uneven idle."
    ],
    "vulnerabilities": [
      "Extremely high labor cost for chain replacement. Since the timing drive is on the transmission side, replacement is almost impossible without pulling the engine. Replacing a stretched chain places a huge financial burden on the owner.",
      "Total immobility due to hybrid failure. The vehicle completely lacks a traditional 12-volt starter motor. In the event of any 48-volt hybrid circuit voltage drop, the car instantly becomes incapable of moving.",
      "Emission-related start prevention countdown. In the event of even a minor sensor fault in the AdBlue system, the computer triggers a lockout. After the permitted number of starts has run out, the vehicle will not restart until serviced.",
      "Particulate filter clogging during urban use. The engine can only perform active DPF regeneration during highway driving. Dense urban traffic and short trips fatally ruin the expensive filter unit.",
      "Engine oil dilution by diesel fuel. During interrupted DPF cleaning cycles, unburnt fuel enters the crankcase. The diluted engine oil drastically loses its lubricating ability, which destroys the engine bearings.",
      "Tandem pump leakage at the firewall. The seal of the combined oil and vacuum pump at the rear end of the engine can fatigue. The leaking oil drips onto the bell housing, and accessing and repairing it is a highly labor-intensive task."
    ],
