    "timingType": "Chain. The M256 engine utilizes a complex timing chain system located at the REAR of the engine block. While generally robust, stretching can occur at high mileages if oil changes are neglected, requiring a massive engine-out or transmission-out repair.",
    "injectionType": "Direct Injection with highly precise Piezo injectors. Combined with a massive 163 hp electric motor integrated into the transmission. The direct-injected nature introduces a severe risk of carbon buildup on the intake valves over time.",
    "engineLifespan": "200 000 - 400 000+ km. The all-aluminum inline-6 block with Nanoslide cylinder coating is mechanically incredibly durable. The true lifespan is entirely dictated by the rigorous maintenance of the High-Voltage battery system, thermal management, and the rear-mounted timing chain.",
    "turboType": "Single Exhaust Gas Turbocharger + Electric Auxiliary Compressor. This sophisticated setup physically eliminates turbo lag. The electric compressor provides instant boost before the traditional exhaust turbo spools up for massive top-end power.",
    "ecuType": "Bosch MG1 combined with an advanced Hybrid Control Module. The system seamlessly juggles pure electric driving (up to ~100km), aggressive Race Start launches, and full ICE power. It is heavily locked down due to the hybrid integration.",
    "euroStandard": "Euro 6e",
    "maxPowerStockInternals": "700+ hp. The internal forged rotating assembly is incredibly strong and perfectly balanced. The primary limitations are the high-voltage battery discharge limits, thermal management, and transmission wet clutch integration.",
