    "timingType": "Simplex timing chain. The M274 utilizes a single-row timing chain located at the front of the engine. The hydraulic tensioners and VVT (Variable Valve Timing) phasers frequently lose pressure, causing a distinct metallic rattle on cold starts. Preventative tensioner replacement is strongly recommended to prevent chain stretch.",
    "injectionType": "Direct Injection operating at up to 200 bar via advanced Piezo injectors. While providing immense low-end torque and excellent fuel economy, the direct-injected nature introduces a severe risk of thick carbon sludge buildup on the intake valves over time.",
    "engineLifespan": "150 000 - 250 000+ km. The M274 block has a highly controversial reliability record. While the infamous wrist pin failures were largely resolved by the late facelift years, the engine remains highly vulnerable to catastrophic piston cracking caused by Low-Speed Pre-Ignition (LSPI). The true lifespan is heavily dictated by rigorous oil changes.",
    "turboType": "Single Exhaust Gas Turbocharger. It provides excellent low-end torque, completely replacing the older 1.8L architectures. The turbocharger itself is generally reliable, but the electronic wastegate actuator is known to fail due to intense heat exposure.",
    "ecuType": "Bosch MED17.7.2. A highly advanced engine control unit managing both the direct injection and variable boost pressure. It is incredibly receptive to software tuning, safely unlocking significant power from the 2.0L block.",
