    "timingType": "Chain. The M276 utilizes independent timing chains for each cylinder bank. Early iterations are notorious for secondary chain tensioner rattle on cold start. The hydraulic tensioners leak down overnight, causing a brief, sharp metallic rattle. Installing updated tensioners alongside preventative check valves in the cylinder head is mandatory to prevent chain stretch.",
    "injectionType": "Direct Injection (CGI) via highly precise piezo-electric injectors operating at up to 200 bar. While providing excellent efficiency, this introduces the inevitability of thick carbon sludge buildup on the intake valves over time.",
    "engineLifespan": "250 000 - 450 000+ km. Mechanically, the M276 3.5L V6 block is exceptionally robust. Because this specific fleet model is artificially detuned via software from 306 hp down to 252 hp, the internal components are completely unstressed. Lifespan is dictated by fixing the chain tensioners and oil leaks.",
    "turboType": "Naturally Aspirated. It entirely lacks complex turbochargers and intercooler plumbing. This vastly simplifies the engine bay and drastically improves long-term reliability.",
    "ecuType": "Bosch MED17.7.3. A highly advanced ECU managing direct injection. Because this E 300 is merely a software-restricted E 350, aftermarket ECU tuning provides astonishingly massive power gains for a naturally aspirated engine simply by removing the factory throttle limitation.",
