    "oilSpecification": "6.5L 5W-40 Fully Synthetic (MB 229.5). Absolute adherence to strict 10,000 km oil change intervals is mandatory to protect the delicate hydraulic chain tensioners and VVT mechanisms.",
    "commonIssues": [
      "Timing Chain Tensioner Rattle: The most critical flaw of the early M276. The secondary hydraulic chain tensioners lose oil pressure when the engine is off. Upon cold startup, the loose chain slaps against the guides, creating a terrifying rattle for three seconds. Factory check valves must be installed to fix this.",
      "Camshaft Position Sensor Oil Leaks: The four camshaft position sensors are notorious for internal seal failures due to intense engine heat. Oil slowly seeps through the sensor body directly into the engine wiring harness, turning a small leak into a major electrical hazard.",
      "Direct Injection Carbon Buildup: Because fuel is injected directly into the combustion chamber, it never washes the intake valves. Thick, tar-like carbon sludge builds up rapidly on the valves, heavily restricting engine airflow and requiring professional walnut blasting.",
      "High-Pressure Fuel Pump Wear: The camshaft-driven high-pressure fuel pump works immensely hard to support the 200 bar direct injection system. It can wear out internally, causing extended cranking times, severe hesitation, or leaking raw fuel into the engine oil.",
      "Ignition Coil Heat Degradation: The ignition coils are exposed to intense engine bay heat and naturally degrade over time. As they begin to fail, the engine will experience subtle misfires under heavy load, severely hurting performance.",
      "NOx Sensor Failures: Models equipped with the advanced exhaust aftertreatment system frequently suffer from NOx sensor degradation. These sensors are incredibly sensitive to carbon and sulfur, triggering persistent check engine lights when they fail."
    ],
    "vulnerabilities": [
      "ECU Destruction via Oil Wicking: If the leaking camshaft position sensors are completely ignored, capillary action will draw the engine oil through the wiring harness directly into the Bosch ECU. Once the oil floods the delicate circuitry of the control unit, it shorts out, requiring a massively expensive replacement.",
      "Catastrophic Timing Chain Jump: If the cold-start chain rattle is ignored for too long, the timing chains will physically stretch beyond the updated tensioner's limits. The loose chain will eventually jump teeth on the camshaft sprockets, completely ruining the engine's mechanical timing and bending the valves.",
      "Cylinder Scoring from Fuel Dilution: If the high-pressure fuel pump fails and leaks raw gasoline into the crankcase, it instantly destroys the oil's viscosity. This diluted oil cannot protect the cylinder walls, leading to fatal Nanoslide coating scoring and catastrophic engine failure.",
      "Subframe Corrosion Collapse: The rear subframe of the C207 chassis is highly susceptible to severe internal rusting, particularly in areas heavily treated with winter road salts. The structural metal rots from the inside out, often causing the lower control arms to detach abruptly while driving.",
      "Torque Converter Glazing: Bypassing the strict 60,000 km 7G-Tronic transmission fluid service interval guarantees premature degradation of the fluid. This causes the torque converter lockup clutch to glaze, resulting in a harsh shuddering sensation when accelerating at low RPMs.",
      "Vacuum Pump Oil Leaks: The mechanical vacuum pump located at the rear of the cylinder head frequently develops failing seals. This allows engine oil to drip down the back of the engine and onto the transmission bellhousing, often misdiagnosed as a rear main seal leak."
    ],
