    "timingType": "Chain. The M276 utilizes independent timing chains for each cylinder bank. Early iterations are notorious for secondary chain tensioner rattle on cold start. The hydraulic tensioners leak down overnight, causing a brief, sharp metallic rattle. Installing updated tensioners alongside preventative check valves in the cylinder head is mandatory to prevent chain stretch.",
    "injectionType": "Direct Injection (CGI) via highly precise piezo-electric injectors operating at up to 200 bar. While providing excellent efficiency and pushing output past 300 horsepower naturally, this introduces the inevitability of thick carbon sludge buildup on the intake valves over time.",
    "engineLifespan": "250 000 - 450 000+ km. Mechanically, the M276 3.5L V6 block is exceptionally robust. The lack of forced induction means internal components are not heavily stressed. Lifespan is largely dictated by fixing the chain tensioners early, maintaining the direct injection system, and repairing minor oil leaks.",
    "turboType": "Naturally Aspirated. It entirely lacks complex turbochargers, intercooler plumbing, and their associated failure points. This vastly simplifies the engine bay and drastically improves overall long-term mechanical reliability.",
    "ecuType": "Bosch MED17.7.3. A highly advanced ECU managing direct injection and multi-spark ignition. Because this is a naturally aspirated engine operating near its maximum potential, aftermarket ECU tuning provides very minimal power gains.",
    "euroStandard": "Euro 5 / Euro 6",
    "maxPowerStockInternals": "380+ hp. The internal rotating assembly is incredibly strong. The naturally aspirated induction limits the ability to push the block to its breaking point unless expensive custom supercharger kits are utilized.",
