    "oilSpecification": "Approx. 8.0 L fully synthetic low-SAPS engine oil meeting Mercedes-Benz MB 229.51 or equivalent approved diesel specification.",
    "commonIssues": [
      "Oil cooler seal leaks are one of the most famous OM642 weak points and can become expensive because the repair is labor-intensive.",
      "Swirl flap and intake-manifold wear can cause fault codes, roughness, and expensive intake-side repair work with age.",
      "EGR contamination and soot buildup are normal long-term diesel issues and can reduce smoothness and drivability if neglected.",
      "Turbo-side boost leaks or charge-air hose faults can make the engine feel less dense and less refined under load.",
      "Injector imbalance, sealing issues, or uneven combustion can create rough idle, hard starting, or extra diesel clatter.",
      "Thermostat drift is common enough to matter because an OM642 that runs too cool loses efficiency and feels less sorted overall.",
      "Glow plug or glow control-module faults can create cold-start complaints and are a common ageing item on Mercedes diesels.",
      "Automatic transmission condition strongly affects the car’s refinement, so neglected fluid service can make the whole drivetrain feel rougher than it should.",
      "Vacuum-related control issues can affect turbo response and general drivability if hoses or control components age out.",
      "Cooling-system seepage or neglected coolant condition can quietly undermine long-term reliability and thermal stability."
    ],
    "vulnerabilities": [
      "The biggest vulnerability is that the engine can hide developing intake, cooling, or injector problems for a long time before the car feels obviously unhealthy.",
      "Cars used mostly for short trips age much worse than those regularly driven on longer routes, because the diesel system prefers warm, sustained running.",
      "Ignoring thermostat behavior is a costly mistake because under-temperature running affects efficiency and overall diesel cleanliness.",
      "Oil cooler seal issues should be handled early because they become messier and more expensive with time.",
      "Weak diagnostics are dangerous because multiple different systems can create similar drivability symptoms.",
      "Poor transmission maintenance can make a good engine feel significantly less premium than it really is.",
      "A cheap repair approach often creates repeat faults rather than solving the underlying cause."
    ],
