    "engineLifespan": "300 000 - 500 000+ km. Mechanically, the OM656 inline-six block is a masterpiece of modern diesel engineering, featuring a vastly simplified rotating assembly compared to older V6 designs. The true lifespan is entirely dictated by the continuous maintenance of its incredibly complex, fragile exhaust aftertreatment and SCR (AdBlue) systems.",
    "turboType": "Sequential Twin-Turbochargers (Biturbo). Utilizes a smaller high-pressure variable geometry turbocharger for instantaneous low-end response, transitioning seamlessly into a larger low-pressure turbo for massive top-end power. This complex two-stage setup effectively eliminates turbo lag and provides a relentless 600 Nm torque curve.",
    "ecuType": "Bosch MD1. An incredibly advanced, highly complex engine management unit that tightly controls the sequential turbos, 2500-bar fuel injection, Camtronic variable exhaust valve timing, and the intricate AdBlue dosing system. Because this is essentially a software-detuned E 400 d, it responds wonderfully to software tuning.",
