    "timingType": "Simplex timing chain located at the absolute rear of the engine block. While chain durability is a significant improvement over the older OM651, stretching can still occur at high mileages if oil changes are neglected. Because of its rearward position against the firewall, replacing it requires dropping the transmission or hoisting the entire engine.",
    "injectionType": "Common-Rail Direct Injection (CDI) operating at an immense 2,500 bar pressure via highly precise Piezo injectors. This extreme pressure ensures phenomenal fuel atomization and power delivery but makes the fuel system highly sensitive to poor-quality diesel or water contamination.",
    "engineLifespan": "250 000 - 450 000+ km. The all-aluminum block paired with forged steel pistons provides an incredibly strong, thermally stable core architecture. The true lifespan is entirely dictated by strict adherence to oil change intervals to protect the fragile valvetrain and the continuous maintenance of the complex Euro 6 AdBlue emissions systems.",
    "turboType": "Sequential Twin-Turbochargers (Bi-Turbo) with water cooling. Utilizes a smaller high-pressure turbo for instantaneous low-end response, transitioning seamlessly into a larger low-pressure turbo for massive top-end power. This eliminates turbo lag entirely and provides a relentless 500 Nm torque curve from a 2.0L block.",
    "ecuType": "Bosch MD1. An incredibly advanced, highly complex engine management unit that tightly controls the sequential turbos, 2500-bar fuel injection, and the intricate AdBlue dosing system. Responds wonderfully to software tuning, safely unlocking massive torque.",
    "euroStandard": "Euro 6d-TEMP",
    "maxPowerStockInternals": "300+ hp. The incredibly robust aluminum block, combined with heavy-duty forged steel pistons, is massively over-engineered to handle the factory 500 Nm torque. The engine handles significant boost increases effortlessly, with tuning limits dictated strictly by exhaust gas temperatures and DPF flow capacity.",
