    "oilSpecification": "6.5L 5W-30 Fully Synthetic Low-SAPS (MB 229.52). Absolute adherence to strict 10,000 km oil change intervals is absolutely mandatory to protect the highly stressed rocker arms, prevent DPF clogging, and lubricate the rear timing chain.",
    "commonIssues": [
      "Camshaft Rocker Arm Wear: The absolute most critical flaw of the OM654 architecture. The roller cam followers (rocker arms) can wear out rapidly, especially if oil quality degrades. This causes a distinct ticking noise from the top end, which, if ignored, will eventually destroy the camshaft lobes entirely.",
      "Rear Timing Chain Stretch: Mercedes located the single-row timing chain at the absolute rear of the engine. While stronger than previous generations, it still stretches over high mileages, causing a sharp metallic rattling noise on cold starts. Replacing it requires a massively expensive engine-out or transmission-out procedure.",
      "Complex SCR/AdBlue System Failures: The highly advanced Euro 6 emissions system heavily relies on continuous AdBlue injection. The heater element inside the tank, the dosing pump, and the incredibly sensitive NOx sensors frequently fail from thermal stress, triggering a countdown that immobilizes the vehicle.",
      "Engine-Mounted DPF/SCR Thermal Stress: To heat up the emissions system quickly, the DPF and dual SCR catalysts are bolted directly to the side of the engine block. This subjects surrounding sensors and wiring harnesses to extreme radiant heat, causing premature degradation and electrical gremlins.",
      "Tandem Pump Oil Leaks: The combined vacuum and oil pump located at the rear of the engine block is known to develop slow weeping oil leaks over tens of thousands of kilometers. Because it is positioned tightly against the firewall, diagnosing and repairing this leak is a highly labor-intensive nightmare.",
      "EGR Valve and Cooler Clogging: The Exhaust Gas Recirculation (EGR) system aggressively routes dirty exhaust back into the intake to lower emissions. This creates thick, tar-like soot that heavily clogs the EGR cooler and the entire intake manifold over time, requiring periodic physical cleaning."
    ],
    "vulnerabilities": [
      "Catastrophic Valvetrain Failure: If the notorious rocker arm wear is ignored, the roller bearing will seize, and the camshaft lobe will literally grind the follower flat. This fills the engine oil with fine metallic glitter, destroying the main bearings and requiring a completely new cylinder head and camshafts.",
      "AdBlue No-Start Immobilization Countdown: If the main engine computer detects any fault within the SCR emissions system, it immediately initiates a hard, irreversible dashboard countdown. Once the permitted miles or engine starts reach absolute zero, the ECU completely immobilizes the vehicle until fixed.",
      "Engine-Out Timing Chain Replacement Cost: Because the timing chain drive is located at the absolute rear of the engine block, access is virtually impossible while the engine is in the car. If the chain stretches and threatens to jump teeth, mechanics must remove the transmission, turning a wear item into a massive labor bill.",
      "DPF Fatal Blockage from Urban Use: The OM654 requires extremely hot exhaust temperatures for extended periods to perform active regeneration cycles for the Diesel Particulate Filter. If the vehicle is used strictly for short city commutes, the DPF will become fatally blocked with dense soot, requiring an incredibly expensive filter replacement.",
      "Injector Hydrolock: The 2500-bar Piezo direct injectors work under immense pressure and can, in rare cases of fuel contamination, stick completely open. Raw liquid diesel fuel rapidly fills the combustion chamber, causing a violent hydrolock that instantly bends the forged connecting rod and destroys the block.",
      "Coolant Intrusion via EGR Cooler: The internal passages of the EGR cooler can crack due to intense thermal cycling, allowing engine coolant to slowly leak directly into the exhaust stream or intake tract. This causes mysterious coolant loss and thick white exhaust smoke, eventually leading to overheating."
    ],
