    "timingType": "Simplex timing chain located at the absolute rear of the engine block. While chain durability is vastly improved in the OM654M architecture, stretching can still occur at extremely high mileages. Because of its rearward position, replacing it requires dropping the transmission or hoisting the entire engine.",
    "injectionType": "Common-Rail Direct Injection (CDI) operating at an absolutely staggering 2,700 bar pressure via highly precise Piezo injectors. This extreme pressure pushes the boundaries of diesel technology, ensuring phenomenal fuel atomization but making the fuel system terrifyingly sensitive to poor-quality diesel.",
    "engineLifespan": "250 000 - 450 000+ km. The core architecture of the OM654M, with its longer stroke and steel pistons, is incredibly strong. However, the true lifespan is entirely dictated by the continuous maintenance of its incredibly complex 48V ISG mild-hybrid system, the fragile valvetrain, and the Euro 6d emissions peripherals.",
    "turboType": "Sequential Twin-Turbochargers with dual water-cooling circuits. Utilizes two highly advanced variable-geometry turbochargers specifically tailored to integrate seamlessly with the electric torque-fill of the 48V ISG. This eliminates turbo lag entirely and provides a relentless 550 Nm torque curve.",
    "ecuType": "Bosch MD1 heavily integrated with the 48V Hybrid Control Module. The system seamlessly juggles the 200 Nm electric torque fill, aggressive engine start/stop cycles, and full ICE power. It responds to software tuning, though limits are dictated by the ISG integration.",
    "euroStandard": "Euro 6d",
    "maxPowerStockInternals": "330+ hp. The incredibly robust aluminum block, combined with heavy-duty forged steel pistons, is massively over-engineered. The engine handles significant boost increases effortlessly, with tuning limits dictated strictly by the 48V ISG electronics and transmission clutches.",
    "fuelConsumption": {
      "city": "6.0 - 7.5 L/100km",
      "highway": "4.5 - 5.5 L/100km",
      "mixed": "5.2 - 6.2 L/100km",
      "sporty": "8.0+ L/100km"
    },
    "oilSpecification": "6.5L 5W-30 Fully Synthetic Low-SAPS (MB 229.52). Absolute adherence to strict 10,000 km oil change intervals is absolutely mandatory to protect the highly stressed rocker arms, lubricate the rear timing chain, and combat minor oil dilution from hybrid start/stop cycling.",
    "commonIssues": [
      "48V ISG (EQ Boost) Failure: The 2nd-generation Integrated Starter Generator is highly complex. If the 48V system, its inverter, or the battery fails, the car loses its starter motor and hybrid assist entirely. The vehicle will be completely immobilized.",
      "Camshaft Rocker Arm Wear: Despite revisions, the roller cam followers (rocker arms) can still wear out rapidly if oil quality degrades. This causes a distinct ticking noise from the top end, which, if ignored, will eventually destroy the camshaft lobes entirely.",
      "Complex SCR/AdBlue System Failures: The highly advanced Euro 6d emissions system heavily relies on continuous AdBlue injection. The heater element inside the tank, the dosing pump, and the incredibly sensitive NOx sensors frequently fail from thermal stress, triggering a no-start countdown.",
      "Engine-Mounted DPF/SCR Thermal Stress: To heat up the emissions system quickly, the massive DPF and dual SCR catalysts are bolted directly to the side of the engine block. This subjects surrounding sensors and wiring harnesses to extreme radiant heat, causing premature electrical degradation.",
      "Rear Timing Chain Stretch: Mercedes retained the single-row timing chain at the absolute rear of the engine. It can still stretch over high mileages, causing a sharp metallic rattling noise on cold starts. Replacing it requires a massively expensive engine-out or transmission-out procedure.",
      "Tandem Pump Oil Leaks: The combined vacuum and oil pump located at the rear of the engine block is known to develop slow weeping oil leaks over tens of thousands of kilometers. Because it is positioned tightly against the firewall, diagnosing and repairing this leak is a highly labor-intensive nightmare."
    ],
    "vulnerabilities": [
      "48V System Immobilization: If the 48V battery or the transmission-mounted ISG fails, the vehicle will be completely immobilized and refuse to start. Independent shops often cannot perform these repairs, requiring a highly expensive tow to the dealership.",
      "Catastrophic Valvetrain Failure: If the notorious rocker arm wear is ignored, the roller bearing will seize, and the camshaft lobe will literally grind the follower flat. This fills the engine oil with fine metallic glitter, destroying the main bearings and requiring a completely new cylinder head.",
      "AdBlue No-Start Immobilization Countdown: If the main engine computer detects any fault within the strictly regulated Euro 6d SCR emissions system, it immediately initiates a hard, irreversible dashboard countdown. Once the permitted miles reach zero, the ECU completely immobilizes the vehicle.",
      "Engine-Out Timing Chain Replacement Cost: Because the timing chain drive is located at the absolute rear of the engine block, access is virtually impossible while the engine is in the car. If the chain stretches and threatens to jump teeth, mechanics must completely remove the transmission assembly.",
      "DPF Fatal Blockage from Urban Use: The OM654M requires extremely hot exhaust temperatures for extended periods to perform active regeneration cycles. If the vehicle is used strictly for short city commutes, the DPF will become fatally blocked with dense soot.",
      "Catastrophic Injector Hydrolock: The 2700-bar Piezo direct injectors work under immense, industry-leading pressure and can stick completely open if contaminated. Raw liquid diesel fuel rapidly fills the combustion chamber, causing a violent hydrolock that instantly bends the forged connecting rod."
    ],
