        "timingType": "Simplex timing chain located at the absolute rear of the engine block against the firewall. By moving to an inline-six architecture, Mercedes placed the timing drive at the back to save space. While the chain itself is highly robust and bathed in oil, any necessary replacements due to high-mileage stretching require a massively expensive engine-out or transmission-out procedure.",
        "injectionType": "Direct Injection (CGI) via highly precise piezo-electric injectors operating at high pressure. This ensures perfect fuel atomization for maximum power and efficiency, but intrinsically introduces the inevitability of thick carbon sludge buildup on the intake valves over prolonged ownership.",
        "engineLifespan": "250 000 - 400 000+ km. Mechanically, the all-aluminum inline-six block and forged rotating assembly are masterpieces of modern AMG engineering, perfectly balanced and incredibly robust. The true lifespan of the vehicle is entirely dictated by the continuous maintenance of its incredibly complex 48V mild-hybrid electrical systems and thermal management components.",
        "turboType": "Single Exhaust Gas Turbocharger + Electric Auxiliary Compressor (eZV). This incredibly advanced dual-charger system completely eliminates turbo lag. The 48V electric compressor instantly forces air into the engine off idle, bridging the gap seamlessly until the massive exhaust gas turbocharger spools up for phenomenal top-end power.",
        "ecuType": "Bosch MG1 heavily integrated with the advanced 48V Hybrid Control Module. The system seamlessly juggles the instant electric torque fill, aggressive engine start/stop cycles, and massive ICE power. It responds incredibly well to software tuning, unlocking true supercar performance.",
        "euroStandard": "Euro 6d-TEMP / Euro 6d",
        "maxPowerStockInternals": "600+ hp. The incredibly robust aluminum block, combined with heavy-duty forged steel internals, is massively over-engineered to handle extreme cylinder pressures. The engine handles significant boost increases effortlessly, with tuning limits dictated strictly by the 48V ISG electronics and the AMG TCT 9G transmission clutches.",
        "fuelConsumption": {
          "city": "11.0 - 13.5 L/100km",
          "highway": "7.5 - 9.0 L/100km",
          "mixed": "8.8 - 10.5 L/100km",
          "sporty": "15.0+ L/100km"
        },
        "oilSpecification": "8.0L 5W-40 Fully Synthetic (MB 229.5 or MB 229.51). Absolute adherence to strict 10,000 km oil change intervals is absolutely mandatory to protect the highly stressed rear timing chain, the twin charging systems, and the delicate 48V ISG integration.",
        "commonIssues": [
          "48V ISG (EQ Boost) System Failure: The 48-volt Integrated Starter Generator system is incredibly complex and serves as the literal heartbeat of the M256. If the 48V battery, the DC/DC converter, or the ISG unit itself fails, the vehicle loses its starter motor entirely. This completely immobilizes the car and results in an astronomically expensive repair bill at the dealership.",
          "Electric Auxiliary Compressor (eZV) Faults: The electric supercharger operates under immense stress to provide instant boost off the line. When its internal electronics or high-speed bearings degrade, the car experiences severe hesitation and triggers Limp Mode. This highly proprietary sealed unit costs a fortune to replace when it fails.",
          "Rear Timing Chain Stretch: Mercedes unfortunately located the single-row timing chain at the absolute rear of the inline-six block. While much stronger than older 4-cylinder chains, it can still physically stretch over very high mileages, causing a metallic rattle on cold starts. Replacing it requires a financially devastating engine-out or transmission-out procedure.",
          "Direct Injection Carbon Buildup: Because fuel is injected directly into the cylinders, it never washes over the intake valves to keep them clean. Over time, thick, tar-like carbon sludge builds up rapidly on the valve stems, causing random misfires and heavily restricting engine airflow. Professional walnut blasting is required to restore peak performance.",
          "Complex Thermal Management Leaks: The M256 utilizes a massive network of mechanical and electric water pumps to cool the engine, the exhaust turbo, the electric turbo, and the 48V battery. The fragile plastic coolant lines and electronic thermostat housings frequently develop slow leaks. Overheating this highly strung AMG engine will warp the aluminum block instantly.",
          "Dynamic Engine Mount Collapse: The active, liquid-filled hydraulic engine mounts are subjected to the immense weight of the inline-six and the brutal 520 Nm of torque. Over tens of thousands of kilometers, the rubber tears and the internal hydraulic fluid leaks out. This causes a harsh vibration to resonate through the steering wheel and cabin while idling in gear."
        ],
        "vulnerabilities": [
          "Total 48V Immobilization: The vehicle relies entirely on the 48V ISG to start the engine, meaning there is no traditional 12V starter motor. If any component within the highly sensitive 48-volt circuit detects a fatal error, the ECU immediately locks out the ignition sequence. You will be completely stranded on the side of the road until a flatbed tow truck arrives.",
          "Engine-Out Timing Chain Replacement Cost: Because the timing chain drive is located at the absolute rear of the long inline-six block, access is virtually impossible while the engine is in the car. If the chain stretches and threatens to jump teeth, mechanics must completely remove the engine and transmission assembly. This turns a standard wear item into a massive labor bill.",
          "Catastrophic eZV Compressor Destruction: If the internal bearings of the electric auxiliary compressor shatter at 70,000 RPM, the resulting metal shrapnel will be violently sucked directly into the engine's intake tract. This catastrophic ingestion instantly destroys the intake valves, scars the cylinder walls, and requires a total engine rebuild.",
          "Cylinder Scoring from Fuel Dilution: The incredibly precise direct injection system operates at massive pressures. If a piezo injector becomes stuck open, raw liquid gasoline washes the lubricating oil off the Nanoslide cylinder walls. This lack of lubrication causes immediate, fatal scoring of the aluminum block, requiring a complete engine replacement.",
          "Transmission Torque Overload: The massive combined torque of the ICE and electric motor places immense, continuous mechanical strain on the AMG SPEEDSHIFT TCT 9G transmission clutches. If the strict 60,000-kilometer fluid service interval is bypassed, the fluid degrades rapidly under the immense heat, guaranteeing premature clutch pack failure.",
          "Subframe Corrosion Collapse: The rear subframe of the C238 chassis is highly susceptible to severe internal rusting, particularly in regions using heavy winter road salts. The structural metal rots entirely from the inside out, often causing the lower control arms to detach abruptly while driving at speed."
        ],
