              "timingType": "Simplex timing chain located at the front of the engine block. The M264 represents a heavy revision over the older M274. The timing system is generally more robust, though the hydraulic tensioners can still experience leak-down overnight, causing a brief metallic rattle on cold starts.",
              "injectionType": "Direct Injection (CGI) operating via highly precise piezo-electric injectors. This extremely high-pressure system ensures perfect atomization for the twin-scroll turbocharger, but inherently introduces thick carbon sludge buildup on the intake valves over long-term ownership.",
              "engineLifespan": "200 000 - 350 000+ km. Mechanically, the all-aluminum block and forged internals are heavily engineered. However, the true lifespan and reliability are overwhelmingly dictated by the continuous maintenance of its incredibly complex 48V EQ Boost mild-hybrid electrical system and water pump assemblies.",
              "turboType": "Single Twin-Scroll Turbocharger. The twin-scroll design drastically reduces exhaust pulse interference, accelerating spool times. Combined with the immediate 150 Nm electric torque fill from the 48V EQ Boost system, turbo lag is virtually eliminated.",
              "ecuType": "Bosch MED17.7.5 heavily integrated with the advanced 48V Hybrid Control Module. The system seamlessly juggles the instant electric torque fill, aggressive engine start/stop cycles, and ICE power. It responds excellently to software tuning.",
              "euroStandard": "Euro 6d-TEMP",
              "maxPowerStockInternals": "360+ hp. The internal forged connecting rods and cast aluminum block are robust, but limits are strictly dictated by the 48V ISG electronics, the transmission torque converter limits, and the threat of LSPI (Low-Speed Pre-Ignition) under excessive boost.",
              "fuelConsumption": {
                "city": "8.5 - 10.5 L/100km",
                "highway": "5.8 - 7.5 L/100km",
                "mixed": "6.8 - 8.5 L/100km",
                "sporty": "11.5+ L/100km"
              },
              "oilSpecification": "6.0L 5W-40 Fully Synthetic (MB 229.5 or 229.51). Absolute adherence to strict 10,000 km oil change intervals is absolutely mandatory to protect the highly stressed timing chain, twin-scroll turbo, and combat oil dilution from hybrid start/stop cycling.",
              "commonIssues": [
                "48V EQ Boost System Failure: The 48-volt belt-driven starter generator system is highly complex. If the 48V battery, the DC/DC converter, or the EQ Boost unit itself fails, the vehicle loses its starter entirely. This immobilizes the car and results in an incredibly expensive repair bill.",
                "Water Pump Failure: The M264 utilizes a highly complex, electronically controlled mechanical water pump that frequently cracks or fails internally. This causes slow, persistent coolant leaks or immediate overheating if the electronic control unit jams.",
                "Direct Injection Carbon Buildup: Because fuel is injected directly into the cylinders, it never washes over the intake valves to keep them clean. Over time, thick, tar-like carbon sludge builds up rapidly on the valve stems, causing random misfires and heavily restricting engine airflow.",
                "PCV Valve Assembly Failure: The crankcase ventilation valve is prone to failing and passing excessive, unmetered oil vapor into the intake tract. This failure coats the entire intercooler and intake manifold in a thick layer of oil, dramatically lowering the effective octane of the fuel.",
                "Timing Chain Tensioner Rattle: The hydraulic chain tensioners can eventually lose their ability to hold oil pressure overnight. This causes a terrifying metallic rattle on cold starts as the loose chain slaps the plastic guides.",
                "High-Pressure Fuel Pump Wear: The camshaft-driven high-pressure fuel pump works immensely hard to support the direct injection system. It can wear out internally, causing extended cranking times and potentially leaking raw fuel into the oil pan."
              ],
              "vulnerabilities": [
                "Total 48V Immobilization: The vehicle relies on the 48V EQ Boost system to start the engine. If any component within the highly sensitive 48-volt circuit detects a fatal error, the ECU immediately locks out the ignition sequence. You will be completely stranded until a flatbed tow truck arrives.",
                "Catastrophic Engine Failure via LSPI: While more resistant than the M274, the M264 is still vulnerable to Low-Speed Pre-Ignition (LSPI). This is a terrifying phenomenon where oil vapors or low-octane fuel detonate prematurely, violently shattering the fragile cast aluminum pistons.",
                "Catastrophic Timing Chain Jump: If the cold-start chain rattle is ignored for too long, the timing chain will physically stretch beyond the tensioner's limits. The loose chain will jump teeth on the camshaft sprockets, causing the pistons to strike the open valves.",
                "Cylinder Scoring from Fuel Dilution: If the high-pressure fuel pump fails and leaks raw gasoline into the crankcase, it instantly destroys the oil's viscosity. This diluted oil cannot protect the Nanoslide cylinder walls, leading to fatal scoring.",
                "Rear Main Seal Blowout: If the PCV system fails entirely and clogs, the resulting crankcase pressure has nowhere to safely vent. This extreme pressure will forcefully blow out the rear main seal, dumping the engine's oil supply between the engine and transmission.",
                "Subframe Corrosion Collapse: The rear subframe of the C238 chassis is highly susceptible to severe internal rusting, particularly in areas heavily treated with winter road salts. The structural metal rots from the inside out, often causing the lower control arms to detach abruptly."
              ],
