                "injectionType": "Direct Injection (CGI) operating at up to 200 bar via advanced Piezo injectors. While providing excellent low-end torque and efficiency, the direct-injected nature introduces a severe risk of thick carbon sludge buildup on the intake valves over time.",
                "engineLifespan": "150 000 - 250 000+ km. The M274 block has a highly controversial reliability record. While the infamous wrist pin failures were largely resolved by the C238's production years, the engine remains highly vulnerable to catastrophic piston cracking caused by Low-Speed Pre-Ignition (LSPI). True lifespan is heavily dictated by rigorous maintenance.",
                "turboType": "Single Exhaust Gas Turbocharger. Spools rapidly to provide excellent mid-range torque, perfectly suiting the heavy coupe. The turbocharger itself is generally reliable, but the electronic wastegate actuator is known to fail due to extreme localized heat exposure.",
